Take this.

1254
00:59:10.560 --> 00:59:13.062
Take this. Put it back.

1255
00:59:23.171 --> 00:59:25.608
If anything happens.
you take this.

1256
00:59:25.707 --> 00:59:27.677
and you stab him
in the neck as hard

1257
00:59:27.776 --> 00:59:28.910
and as fast as you can.

1258
00:59:29.010 --> 00:59:30.213
-No! No. no!
-It has to be you.

1259
00:59:30.313 --> 00:59:31.481
He's watching me too closely.

1260
00:59:31.581 --> 00:59:33.851
-He won't expect us to do it.
-Sister. no!

1261
00:59:33.950 --> 00:59:35.351
Okay. Let's have a code word.

1262
00:59:35.450 --> 00:59:36.686
Okay? Um...

1263
00:59:36.785 --> 00:59:38.653
Hey. if I say
"magic underwear."

1264
00:59:38.755 --> 00:59:40.590
that means stab. Okay?

1265
00:59:41.356 --> 00:59:42.358
(DISTANT THUD)

1266
00:59:42.457 --> 00:59:44.193
He's coming.

1267
00:59:44.293 --> 00:59:46.896
Magic underwear.
That's the code word. Okay?

1268
00:59:46.995 --> 00:59:48.164
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1269
00:59:50.700 --> 00:59:52.368
(CREAKING)

1270
00:59:53.369 --> 00:59:54.637
(PAXTON WHIMPERS)

1271
00:59:55.571 --> 00:59:57.305
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

1272
01:00:02.912 --> 01:00:03.881
(DOOR OPENS)

1273
01:00:03.979 --> 01:00:06.182
(CREAKING)

1274
01:00:08.216 --> 01:00:10.620
(CREAKING CONTINUES)

1275
01:00:16.559 --> 01:00:18.794
-(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)
-(BOTH BREATHING HEAVILY)

1276
01:00:18.896 --> 01:00:20.095
Mr. Reed?

1277
01:00:20.963 --> 01:00:23.198
(OMINOUS MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1278
01:00:25.568 --> 01:00:27.970
(SQUELCHY FOOTSTEPS)

1279
01:00:30.106 --> 01:00:32.175
(LANTERN CREAKING)

1280
01:00:35.111 --> 01:00:37.245
-(WHIMPERS)
-Mrs. Reed?

1281
01:00:38.916 --> 01:00:40.216
Is that you?

1282
01:00:44.787 --> 01:00:46.555
(OMINOUS MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1283
01:00:54.997 --> 01:00:57.200
(PAXTON WHIMPERING)

1284
01:00:59.168 --> 01:01:00.403
(BARNES INHALES SHARPLY)

1285
01:01:00.503 --> 01:01:01.504
(PAXTON GASPS)

1286
01:01:03.706 --> 01:01:05.675
(BONES CRACKING)

1287
01:01:12.981 --> 01:01:14.649
What's happening to her?

1288
01:01:15.517 --> 01:01:17.153
(RATTLE)

1289
01:01:17.253 --> 01:01:19.421
<i>(CREEP</i> BY RADIOHEAD PLAYING)

1290
01:01:25.863 --> 01:01:26.796
(MR. REED MOCKINGLY SINGING)

1291
01:01:26.897 --> 01:01:28.097
<i>♪ But I'm a creep ♪</i>

1292
01:01:28.764 --> 01:01:30.934
<i>♪ I'm a weirdo ♪</i>

1293
01:01:31.033 --> 01:01:32.133
(MR. REED LAUGHING)

1294
01:01:32.235 --> 01:01:33.669
BARNES: Mr. Reed?

1295
01:01:36.874 --> 01:01:38.106
BARNES: Where are you?

1296
01:01:38.207 --> 01:01:40.376
-(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)
-(MR. REED HUMS ALONG)

1297
01:01:43.479 --> 01:01:45.615
<i>♪ Couldn't look you</i>
<i>in the eye ♪</i>

1298
01:01:49.084 --> 01:01:51.454
<i>♪ You're just like an angel ♪</i>

1299
01:01:54.090 --> 01:01:55.124
(FIRE CRACKLING)

1300
01:01:55.224 --> 01:01:57.793
<i>♪ Your skin makes me cry ♪</i>

1301
01:01:58.693 --> 01:02:01.030
(SCRAPING)

1302
01:02:04.033 --> 01:02:06.003
(GROANING. WHEEZING)

1303
01:02:12.976 --> 01:02:14.243
(SHUSHES)

1304
01:02:14.343 --> 01:02:15.979
(MOUTHING IMPERCEPTIBLY)

1305
01:02:16.077 --> 01:02:18.214
(WHIMPERING SOFTLY)

1306
01:02:19.782 --> 01:02:21.216
(MOUTHING) No.

1307
01:02:22.450 --> 01:02:24.120
(OBJECTS CLANKING IN DISTANCE)

1308
01:02:24.220 --> 01:02:26.589
<i>♪ And I'm a creep ♪</i>

1309
01:02:28.926 --> 01:02:30.392
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1310
01:02:30.493 --> 01:02:32.794
(WOMAN WHISPERING
INDISTINCTLY)

1311
01:02:39.035 --> 01:02:41.202
(PANTING)

1312
01:02:47.476 --> 01:02:50.345
-(MR. REED HUMMING)
<i>-(CREEP</i> CONTINUES PLAYING)

1313
01:02:51.546 --> 01:02:53.115
(PANTING)

1314
01:02:53.215 --> 01:02:54.182
(RATTLING)

1315
01:02:54.283 --> 01:02:55.785
<i>♪ I wanna have control ♪</i>

1316
01:02:59.220 --> 01:03:01.090
<i>♪ I want a perfect body ♪</i>

1317
01:03:01.189 --> 01:03:03.526
(SCRAPING)

1318
01:03:04.427 --> 01:03:06.128
(SCRAPING.
THUDDING BEHIND DOOR)

1319
01:03:06.227 --> 01:03:09.231
<i>♪ I want a perfect soul ♪</i>

1320
01:03:10.834 --> 01:03:13.535
<i>♪ I want you to notice ♪</i>

1321
01:03:16.405 --> 01:03:18.140
<i>♪ When I'm not around ♪</i>

1322
01:03:18.240 --> 01:03:20.610
(LOUD BANGING)

1323
01:03:21.912 --> 01:03:24.881
♪ <i>You're so very special ♪</i>

1324
01:03:28.017 --> 01:03:30.218
♪ <i>But I'm a creep ♪</i>

1325
01:03:33.990 --> 01:03:36.860
<i>♪ I'm a weirdo ♪</i>

1326
01:03:39.062 --> 01:03:42.398
<i>♪ What the hell</i>
<i>am I doin' here? ♪</i>

1327
01:03:45.234 --> 01:03:47.135
♪ <i>I don't belong here ♪</i>

1328
01:03:47.236 --> 01:03:48.803
-(TAPE PLAYER SCREECHES)
<i>-(CREEP</i> STOPS PLAYING)

1329
01:03:51.506 --> 01:03:52.976
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>I had to be sure</i>

1330
01:03:53.075 --> 01:03:54.610
<i>before I introduced you</i>
<i>to her.</i>

1331
01:03:55.644 --> 01:03:58.147
Sure about what?
(BREATH TREMBLING)

1332
01:03:58.247 --> 01:04:00.182
You are now in the presence

1333
01:04:01.084 --> 01:04:03.218
of a living prophet of God.

1334
01:04:03.318 --> 01:04:05.655
(WOMAN WHISPERING
INDISTINCTLY)

1335
01:04:11.293 --> 01:04:13.562
-(WOMAN WHEEZING)
-(BONES CRACKING)

1336
01:04:20.736 --> 01:04:22.139
MR. REED: <i>The reason</i>
<i>I invited you</i>

1337
01:04:22.238 --> 01:04:24.372
<i>into my sanctuary tonight</i>
<i>is because</i>

1338
01:04:24.473 --> 01:04:26.274
<i>I have been shown a miracle.</i>

1339
01:04:27.476 --> 01:04:28.845
<i>I believe</i>
<i>this miracle is proof</i>

1340
01:04:28.945 --> 01:04:31.781
<i>that all known religions</i>
<i>are demonstrably false.</i>

1341
01:04:31.881 --> 01:04:36.419
<i>and only an ancient echo</i>
<i>of something true.</i>

1342
01:04:38.155 --> 01:04:39.856
<i>I need a witness.</i>

1343
01:04:39.956 --> 01:04:44.392
<i>you. to verify</i>
<i>that the miracle is real.</i>

1344
01:04:46.227 --> 01:04:48.430
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

1345
01:04:58.975 --> 01:05:01.878
<i>Now. our family recipe</i>
<i>for blueberry pie is.</i>

1346
01:05:01.977 --> 01:05:03.479
<i>I think. a traditional one.</i>

1347
01:05:03.579 --> 01:05:06.716
The ingredients include
butter. flour. corn starch.

1348
01:05:06.816 --> 01:05:08.151
sugar. lemon.

1349
01:05:08.249 --> 01:05:10.120
blueberries. of course.

1350
01:05:10.218 --> 01:05:13.090
but tonight I've also included
some wolf's bane

1351
01:05:13.189 --> 01:05:14.523
and some belladonna.

1352
01:05:15.557 --> 01:05:18.760
which means that.
in a short while.

1353
01:05:20.595 --> 01:05:24.101
the Prophet will be dead
from consuming the pie.

1354
01:05:24.200 --> 01:05:26.368
(SQUELCHING)

1355
01:05:27.436 --> 01:05:28.470
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>Then.</i>

1356
01:05:28.571 --> 01:05:31.539
<i>you will witness a miracle.</i>

1357
01:05:33.209 --> 01:05:35.377
By the grace of God.

1358
01:05:36.847 --> 01:05:38.247
she will be resurrected.

1359
01:05:38.747 --> 01:05:40.950
(WHEEZING WEAKLY)

1360
01:05:46.622 --> 01:05:48.959
(CONTINUES WHEEZING WEAKLY)

1361
01:06:09.345 --> 01:06:11.313
-(RETCHES)
-(LANTERN CLATTERS)

1362
01:06:16.485 --> 01:06:17.954
Now. feel her pulse. please.

1363
01:06:19.388 --> 01:06:20.555
Both of you.

1364
01:06:21.892 --> 01:06:23.526
(WATER DRIPPING)

1365
01:06:23.626 --> 01:06:24.928
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>I need you</i>

1366
01:06:25.028 --> 01:06:27.428
<i>to feel her pulse right now!</i>

1367
01:06:31.432 --> 01:06:32.836
(PAXTON BREATHING HEAVILY)

1368
01:06:32.936 --> 01:06:34.503
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>Acknowledge. please.</i>

1369
01:06:34.602 --> 01:06:36.639
<i>that her heart has now</i>
<i>stopped pumping.</i>

1370
01:06:36.738 --> 01:06:38.975
<i>Do you know how to do that?</i>

1371
01:06:39.075 --> 01:06:40.776
<i>Index and middle finger</i>
<i>on the side of the neck.</i>

1372
01:06:40.877 --> 01:06:43.914
<i>in the soft. hollow area</i>
<i>just beside the windpipe.</i>

1373
01:06:45.548 --> 01:06:46.917
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1374
01:06:47.017 --> 01:06:49.651
MR. REED: <i>Both of you. please.</i>
<i>lift her head to be sure.</i>

1375
01:06:52.889 --> 01:06:54.557
(SQUELCHING)

1376
01:06:57.026 --> 01:06:59.327
(PAXTON SHUDDERS)

1377
01:07:01.164 --> 01:07:02.131
-(PROPHET GURGLES)
-(PAXTON GASPS)

1378
01:07:02.231 --> 01:07:03.532
PAXTON: She moved! She moved!

1379
01:07:03.631 --> 01:07:06.102
MR. REED: (LAUGHING) <i>That was</i>
<i>just a catalytic spasm.</i>

1380
01:07:06.202 --> 01:07:07.535
PAXTON: (GASPS) She's alive!

1381
01:07:07.635 --> 01:07:09.206
MR. REED: <i>No! No. no. Not yet.</i>

1382
01:07:09.305 --> 01:07:10.874
<i>Chemicals being released</i>
<i>into her body.</i>

1383
01:07:10.974 --> 01:07:12.843
<i>Acknowledge. please.</i>
<i>that there's no pulse.</i>

1384
01:07:12.943 --> 01:07:13.977
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

1385
01:07:14.077 --> 01:07:15.077
<i>Acknowledge!</i>

1386
01:07:15.178 --> 01:07:16.213
-No. No pulse.
-No pulse.

1387
01:07:16.313 --> 01:07:17.446
MR. REED: <i>Thank you.</i>

1388
01:07:17.546 --> 01:07:19.816
<i>Acknowledge that she is</i>
<i>no longer breathing.</i>

1389
01:07:22.351 --> 01:07:23.519
<i>Do you feel a breath?</i>

1390
01:07:28.291 --> 01:07:29.425
BARNES: No. No.

1391
01:07:29.524 --> 01:07:30.559
MR. REED: <i>So she's dead.</i>
BARNES: Yes.

1392
01:07:30.659 --> 01:07:32.428
-(WHIMPERS)
-MR. REED: <i>Okay.</i>

1393
01:07:33.028 --> 01:07:34.563
<i>Thank you.</i>

1394
01:07:34.662 --> 01:07:39.836
<i>A moment longer. and you will</i>
<i>witness a resurrection.</i>

1395
01:07:41.004 --> 01:07:43.572
<i>She'll return</i>
<i>and she will tell us</i>

1396
01:07:43.671 --> 01:07:45.506
<i>what she saw in the afterlife.</i>

1397
01:07:48.245 --> 01:07:49.544
Has the Prophet moved?

1398
01:07:50.247 --> 01:07:51.780
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1399
01:07:51.881 --> 01:07:53.381
No.

1400
01:07:53.481 --> 01:07:54.450
MR. REED OVER SPEAKERS:
<i>Hello?</i>

1401
01:07:54.550 --> 01:07:56.151
-No. No.
-Mmm-mmm.

1402
01:07:56.253 --> 01:07:57.354
(BARNES WHIMPERS)

1403
01:07:57.452 --> 01:08:00.055
MR. REED: <i>All right.</i>
<i>Just</i> un momentino.

1404
01:08:05.128 --> 01:08:06.528
<i>Only a moment longer.</i>

1405
01:08:08.098 --> 01:08:10.033
-(BELL RINGING)
-(GASPS)

1406
01:08:11.901 --> 01:08:13.502
(BREATHING RAPIDLY)
The Elders?

1407
01:08:15.939 --> 01:08:17.974
(DOORBELL RINGS)

1408
01:08:20.408 --> 01:08:22.278
(FOOTSTEPS ECHOING)

1409
01:08:22.378 --> 01:08:24.612
(DOOR LOCKS)

1410
01:08:28.750 --> 01:08:30.920
-(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)
-(BOTH PANTING)

1411
01:08:33.421 --> 01:08:35.456
(PANTING)

1412
01:08:35.556 --> 01:08:37.558
-We scream.
-We scream.

1413
01:08:37.659 --> 01:08:40.029
BARNES: But not until
he answers the door.

1414
01:08:45.901 --> 01:08:47.669
(KNOCKING)

1415
01:08:48.536 --> 01:08:50.072
PAXTON: He's coming back.
BARNES: Scream! Scream!

1416
01:08:50.172 --> 01:08:52.074
(PAXTON AND BARNES SCREAMING)

1417
01:08:52.175 --> 01:08:52.975
(DOOR CREAKING)

1418
01:08:53.075 --> 01:08:55.510
-(DOOR SHUTS)
-(BOTH CONTINUE SCREAMING)

1419
01:08:56.111 --> 01:08:57.146
(LIGHTS CLICK)

1420
01:09:01.016 --> 01:09:02.184
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

1421
01:09:03.986 --> 01:09:05.322
(KNOCKING)

1422
01:09:05.421 --> 01:09:06.755
Coming!

1423
01:09:07.923 --> 01:09:09.925
(TICKING)

1424
01:09:15.264 --> 01:09:16.231
Ah! Sorry!

1425
01:09:16.332 --> 01:09:17.433
I was at the back. (CHUCKLES)

1426
01:09:17.532 --> 01:09:19.335
-No. I'm sorry to bother you.
-No.

1427
01:09:19.435 --> 01:09:20.735
I'm just in the neighborhood
looking for

1428
01:09:20.836 --> 01:09:22.804
two young ladies
from my church.

1429
01:09:22.905 --> 01:09:23.872
Oh.

1430
01:09:24.773 --> 01:09:25.975
Is everything all right?

1431
01:09:26.075 --> 01:09:28.043
(BOTH SCREAMING)

1432
01:09:29.278 --> 01:09:30.611
(BOTH PANTING)

1433
01:09:30.712 --> 01:09:32.514
They can't hear us.

1434
01:09:33.481 --> 01:09:34.682
MAN: <i>I'm sure</i>
<i>everything's fine.</i>

1435
01:09:34.782 --> 01:09:35.985
<i>I was just wondering</i>
<i>if they...</i>

1436
01:09:36.085 --> 01:09:37.052
(WIND BLOWING)

1437
01:09:37.152 --> 01:09:38.120
...stopped by.

1438
01:09:38.220 --> 01:09:39.288
No. I'm sorry to say.

1439
01:09:39.389 --> 01:09:43.258
you are the first house caller
I've had all day. so.

1440
01:09:43.892 --> 01:09:46.195
-Did you see this?
-It's locked.

1441
01:09:50.332 --> 01:09:51.300
BARNES: Help.

1442
01:09:51.400 --> 01:09:52.667
Help.

1443
01:09:52.767 --> 01:09:55.371
We can pull the rug.

1444
01:09:55.471 --> 01:09:56.405
The matches.

1445
01:09:56.505 --> 01:09:58.340
We start a fire.

1446
01:09:58.440 --> 01:09:59.608
smoke out the speaking pipe
to make sure

1447
01:09:59.707 --> 01:10:01.410
the Elder knows we're here.

1448
01:10:01.509 --> 01:10:04.413
Okay. But you did ask

1449
01:10:04.512 --> 01:10:06.782
for more information
on the church. correct?

1450
01:10:06.882 --> 01:10:08.649
Uh. this...
this is the which church?

1451
01:10:08.750 --> 01:10:10.152
The Church of Jesus Christ
of Latter-day Saints.

1452
01:10:10.252 --> 01:10:12.553
Yes. yes. yes. yes.

1453
01:10:12.653 --> 01:10:15.024
(WIND BLOWING)

1454
01:10:15.124 --> 01:10:16.557
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1455
01:10:16.657 --> 01:10:19.094
BARNES: Pull. Careful.

1456
01:10:24.500 --> 01:10:26.101
Is there some other way
I can help?

1457
01:10:26.201 --> 01:10:28.170
Do you want to use my phone.
call the police?

1458
01:10:28.270 --> 01:10:29.872
-I could get my coat...
-No. no. That's fine.

1459
01:10:29.972 --> 01:10:31.073
...and come help you
look around.

1460
01:10:31.173 --> 01:10:32.740
No. no. no. no. no.
I'm sure they're not far.

1461
01:10:33.475 --> 01:10:34.575
Uh. thank you for your time.

1462
01:10:34.675 --> 01:10:37.179
All right. well. good luck.
Yeah. I mean that.

1463
01:10:37.279 --> 01:10:38.613
-Okay.
-Uh-huh.

1464
01:10:39.349 --> 01:10:40.816
(WIND BLOWING)

1465
01:10:42.418 --> 01:10:44.619
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1466
01:10:54.463 --> 01:10:56.731
-(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)
-(DOOR CREAKS)

1467
01:11:02.371 --> 01:11:03.439
(CREAKING)

1468
01:11:03.539 --> 01:11:05.374
(FOOTSTEPS)

1469
01:11:05.474 --> 01:11:07.042
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1470
01:11:07.142 --> 01:11:08.177
(CLICKS)

1471
01:11:09.744 --> 01:11:11.947
(WATER POURING)

1472
01:11:12.981 --> 01:11:13.782
(THUD)

1473
01:11:13.882 --> 01:11:15.451
(FURNITURE DRAGGING)

1474
01:11:15.551 --> 01:11:17.319
(FOOTSTEPS)

1475
01:11:25.527 --> 01:11:26.995
(CLICKING)

1476
01:11:28.264 --> 01:11:29.630
(SCRAPING)

1477
01:11:29.730 --> 01:11:32.067
-(FLOOR CREAKING)
-(FOOTSTEPS)

1478
01:11:42.111 --> 01:11:43.378
(MR. REED COUGHS)

1479
01:11:44.447 --> 01:11:46.081
(MR. REED CLEARS THROAT)

1480
01:11:47.748 --> 01:11:49.650
(OBJECT DRAGS)

1481
01:11:55.324 --> 01:11:56.325
(TENSE MUSIC BUILDS)

1482
01:11:56.425 --> 01:11:57.860
No.

1483
01:12:04.300 --> 01:12:06.268
(CLICKING)

1484
01:12:07.302 --> 01:12:09.037
(FOOTSTEPS)

1485
01:12:09.770 --> 01:12:11.974
(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)

1486
01:12:13.609 --> 01:12:14.877
(BARNES GRUNTS)

1487
01:12:16.979 --> 01:12:18.046
-(THUD)
-(DOOR CREAKS)

1488
01:12:18.148 --> 01:12:19.780
PAXTON: (WHISPERING)
He's coming!

1489
01:12:19.882 --> 01:12:22.117
-(FOOTSTEPS)
-(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1490
01:12:22.618 --> 01:12:24.319
(DOORBELL RINGS)

1491
01:12:24.419 --> 01:12:26.421
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1492
01:12:30.092 --> 01:12:31.193
(RATTLING)

1493
01:12:31.960 --> 01:12:34.695
Yeah? Yeah? Any luck?

1494
01:12:34.795 --> 01:12:36.865
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1495
01:12:43.005 --> 01:12:44.006
(GASPS)

1496
01:12:45.474 --> 01:12:46.909
She moved.

1497
01:12:47.609 --> 01:12:49.311
-What do you mean?
-When we were gone.

1498
01:12:52.747 --> 01:12:54.583
No.
you're remembering it wrong.

1499
01:12:54.682 --> 01:12:55.683
She hasn't moved at all.

1500
01:12:55.783 --> 01:12:56.751
Her head is different.

1501
01:12:56.852 --> 01:12:59.188
-That's where she was!
-It's not!

1502
01:12:59.288 --> 01:13:01.858
Sister. that's not
how I remember it. Please!

1503
01:13:01.957 --> 01:13:04.293
Please. just come on! Help!

1504
01:13:04.993 --> 01:13:06.828
Hold the sleeve up.

1505
01:13:09.465 --> 01:13:14.136
I'd be remiss if I didn't
ask you one question.

1506
01:13:14.836 --> 01:13:16.939
(DRAMATIC MUSIC BUILDS)

1507
01:13:18.440 --> 01:13:19.408
(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1508
01:13:19.508 --> 01:13:21.944
Have you received
this booklet?

1509
01:13:23.245 --> 01:13:24.613
I have not.

1510
01:13:24.712 --> 01:13:27.316
but I will give it a look-see.

1511
01:13:27.416 --> 01:13:29.451
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1512
01:13:29.551 --> 01:13:30.452
PAXTON: Try another.

1513
01:13:30.552 --> 01:13:31.853
BARNES: I know.

1514
01:13:31.954 --> 01:13:34.256
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1515
01:13:37.292 --> 01:13:38.726
Focus.

1516
01:13:38.827 --> 01:13:40.395
(WIND BLOWING)

1517
01:13:42.398 --> 01:13:44.300
(RATTLING)

1518
01:13:44.733 --> 01:13:45.733
Faster.

1519
01:13:45.834 --> 01:13:47.436
(MATCH IGNITES)

1520
01:13:48.303 --> 01:13:49.271
(BARNES WHIMPERS)

1521
01:13:50.439 --> 01:13:52.507
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC BUILDS)

1522
01:14:01.516 --> 01:14:02.750
(GASPS)

1523
01:14:03.652 --> 01:14:04.620
(BARNES GRUNTS)

1524
01:14:04.720 --> 01:14:06.488
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1525
01:14:13.028 --> 01:14:14.264
(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1526
01:14:14.363 --> 01:14:16.298
(WIND GUSTING)

1527
01:14:16.398 --> 01:14:17.399
(MATCH SCRAPING ON WALL)

1528
01:14:20.235 --> 01:14:21.470
(BARNES WHIMPERS)

1529
01:14:21.570 --> 01:14:24.306
(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)

1530
01:14:24.407 --> 01:14:26.475
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

1531
01:14:31.413 --> 01:14:32.381
(MATCH IGNITES)

1532
01:14:32.481 --> 01:14:34.416
-(SCREAMS)
-(GASPS)

1533
01:14:34.516 --> 01:14:36.618
-(BOTH GASPING)
-(WHEEZES)

1534
01:14:36.718 --> 01:14:39.889
-(RETCHES)
-(BOTH GASPING)

1535
01:14:41.823 --> 01:14:42.991
(RETCHES)

1536
01:14:43.091 --> 01:14:44.293
(COUGHS)

1537
01:14:44.393 --> 01:14:46.228
(PROPHET WHEEZES)

1538
01:14:47.929 --> 01:14:50.265
PROPHET: Conductor...

1539
01:14:50.666 --> 01:14:54.536
says... my... name.

1540
01:14:55.270 --> 01:14:58.373
White... clouds.

1541
01:14:58.907 --> 01:15:01.777
Not... Heaven.

1542
01:15:01.877 --> 01:15:05.480
They... unplug...

1543
01:15:06.181 --> 01:15:08.150
my brain.

1544
01:15:09.384 --> 01:15:11.820
It is...

1545
01:15:13.288 --> 01:15:14.289
not...

1546
01:15:14.791 --> 01:15:16.425
real.

1547
01:15:16.525 --> 01:15:17.526
(INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1548
01:15:17.626 --> 01:15:19.861
MR. REED:
And. thank you. Prophet.

1549
01:15:19.961 --> 01:15:21.563
We are very grateful
for your passage

1550
01:15:21.663 --> 01:15:23.166
to the other side.

1551
01:15:23.265 --> 01:15:24.366
(WHEEZING)

1552
01:15:24.466 --> 01:15:28.403
Your prophecy will be recorded
into our liturgical texts.

1553
01:15:28.503 --> 01:15:31.773
Come. You must be exhausted.
Take my arm.

1554
01:15:31.873 --> 01:15:33.875
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1555
01:15:36.511 --> 01:15:38.480
(BARNES BREATHING HEAVILY)

1556
01:15:41.149 --> 01:15:42.317
(INDISTINCT WHISPERING)

1557
01:15:42.417 --> 01:15:44.453
(INAUDIBLE)

1558
01:15:44.553 --> 01:15:46.555
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

1559
01:15:47.322 --> 01:15:48.423
(MATCH SCRAPING)

1560
01:15:50.392 --> 01:15:51.360
(PROPHET WHIMPERS)

1561
01:15:51.460 --> 01:15:52.461
(DOOR CREAKS. SHUTS)

1562
01:15:56.965 --> 01:15:58.200
Well. now.

1563
01:16:00.001 --> 01:16:01.803
You see. this is rather
interesting because...

1564
01:16:01.903 --> 01:16:04.072
-(OBJECT CLANKS)
-(MR. REED CHUCKLES)

1565
01:16:04.172 --> 01:16:08.310
I know that one of you
has been lying

1566
01:16:09.778 --> 01:16:12.114
since you first got here.
(CHUCKLING)

1567
01:16:12.215 --> 01:16:14.349
And do you know
how I know that?

1568
01:16:14.449 --> 01:16:16.051
Excuse me. can I...
can I take that?

1569
01:16:16.151 --> 01:16:18.220
I know from the way

1570
01:16:18.320 --> 01:16:22.425
that the fire reacts
to each of you.

1571
01:16:22.524 --> 01:16:23.492
A.

1572
01:16:25.260 --> 01:16:26.528
B.

1573
01:16:26.628 --> 01:16:28.865
Yeah. One of you has
a very. very... (CHUCKLING)

1574
01:16:28.965 --> 01:16:32.869
...very big secret.
but we will know more soon.

1575
01:16:32.968 --> 01:16:35.270
There will be
before you saw a woman die

1576
01:16:35.370 --> 01:16:38.440
and come back to life.
and there will be after.

1577
01:16:38.541 --> 01:16:40.609
(BLOWS) Books will be written
about it.

1578
01:16:40.709 --> 01:16:44.079
So choose your words
very carefully when I ask.

1579
01:16:44.746 --> 01:16:45.914
what did you witness?

1580
01:16:47.983 --> 01:16:49.251
Tell me. Tell me what you saw.

1581
01:16:50.051 --> 01:16:51.520
How did she...

1582
01:16:51.620 --> 01:16:52.554
I don't know...

1583
01:16:52.654 --> 01:16:54.590
And if you didn't
see something transcendental.

1584
01:16:54.689 --> 01:16:55.757
you absolutely must tell me.

1585
01:16:55.858 --> 01:16:57.426
I don't know.

1586
01:16:57.526 --> 01:16:58.393
'Cause if I'm wrong.

1587
01:16:58.493 --> 01:16:59.928
I need to hear it.
That's why you're here.

1588
01:17:00.028 --> 01:17:01.496
It's a contrived experiment.
We are your prisoners!

1589
01:17:01.596 --> 01:17:03.198
-It doesn't make sense...
-MR. REED: Oh. pooh!

1590
01:17:03.298 --> 01:17:04.366
-We're all prisoners together.
-...for us to have an opinion!

1591
01:17:04.466 --> 01:17:05.467
You must know by now
that any of us can leave

1592
01:17:05.567 --> 01:17:07.870
whenever we want.
but why would we want.

1593
01:17:08.003 --> 01:17:09.104
after what we've seen?

1594
01:17:09.204 --> 01:17:11.606
I saw it. I saw it.

1595
01:17:11.706 --> 01:17:13.141
I heard her describe

1596
01:17:13.241 --> 01:17:14.877
what she experienced
on the other side.

1597
01:17:14.976 --> 01:17:16.880
Great! What did you hear?

1598
01:17:16.978 --> 01:17:20.148
She said
there was a conductor.

1599
01:17:20.248 --> 01:17:22.951
-Yes. Yeah.
-Did she mean angel?

1600
01:17:23.051 --> 01:17:25.454
She had a feeling
of disassociation.

1601
01:17:25.554 --> 01:17:28.291
a feeling that something
wasn't real.

1602
01:17:28.390 --> 01:17:29.425
That's it.

1603
01:17:30.425 --> 01:17:31.393
So now you know.

1604
01:17:32.961 --> 01:17:33.962
Now. we know?

1605
01:17:34.063 --> 01:17:35.363
Yeah. now. you know.

1606
01:17:36.599 --> 01:17:37.566
Know?

1607
01:17:38.800 --> 01:17:40.168
I can show you God.

1608
01:17:41.603 --> 01:17:44.273
If you're willing to die.

1609
01:17:44.372 --> 01:17:47.242
It... it can be painless.
It can be temporary.

1610
01:17:47.342 --> 01:17:49.478
Like the Prophet.
you can be brought back.

1611
01:17:50.545 --> 01:17:52.148
It doesn't have
to be frightening at all.

1612
01:17:52.247 --> 01:17:53.682
I'll tell you... I'll tell you
what's frightening.

1613
01:17:53.782 --> 01:17:55.217
Not knowing is frightening!

1614
01:17:55.317 --> 01:17:56.853
Where do we come from?
What are we doing here?

1615
01:17:56.953 --> 01:17:58.186
What's our purpose?

1616
01:17:58.286 --> 01:18:01.090
The terror of those questions
is why religions exist.

1617
01:18:01.189 --> 01:18:02.959
I can answer
those questions for you.

1618
01:18:03.058 --> 01:18:06.261
I can give you a comfort
no religion in the world

1619
01:18:07.028 --> 01:18:08.331
is capable of giving you.

1620
01:18:10.365 --> 01:18:12.267
It all makes sense now.

1621
01:18:14.402 --> 01:18:16.505
I've been asking myself
all night.

1622
01:18:17.472 --> 01:18:20.041
how is he gonna
make killing us our idea?

1623
01:18:20.141 --> 01:18:21.309
(MR. REED SIGHS)

1624
01:18:23.245 --> 01:18:24.613
Sister Barnes.
you're in a muddle.

1625
01:18:24.713 --> 01:18:25.480
I know. I can't tell

1626
01:18:25.581 --> 01:18:27.550
if you're playing chess
or checkers.

1627
01:18:28.083 --> 01:18:29.718
Monopoly!

1628
01:18:29.819 --> 01:18:30.853
Come on. it was right there.

1629
01:18:30.953 --> 01:18:32.822
You didn't show us a miracle.

1630
01:18:32.922 --> 01:18:34.556
Okay. what did I show you?

1631
01:18:35.157 --> 01:18:36.993
That wasn't a miracle.

1632
01:18:37.092 --> 01:18:38.828
MR. REED: So you say.
What did I show you?

1633
01:18:38.928 --> 01:18:40.930
That was not a miracle!

1634
01:18:41.029 --> 01:18:42.398
What did I show you?

1635
01:18:44.132 --> 01:18:46.668
It was a magic trick.

1636
01:18:48.603 --> 01:18:49.939
MR. REED: A magic trick?

1637
01:18:50.038 --> 01:18:52.240
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1638
01:18:55.277 --> 01:18:58.280
You wanna know why
we don't talk about Taco Bell?

1639
01:18:58.380 --> 01:19:00.115
It killed me
when I was four years old.

1640
01:19:00.215 --> 01:19:03.318
Fifty people were hospitalized
from an E. coli outbreak.

1641
01:19:03.418 --> 01:19:05.287
The kids at school
called me Taco Hell

1642
01:19:05.387 --> 01:19:06.856
'cause I was clinically dead

1643
01:19:06.956 --> 01:19:09.224
while doctors operated
on my kidneys.

1644
01:19:11.660 --> 01:19:13.395
When I was dead.

1645
01:19:13.495 --> 01:19:17.365
I saw exactly
what your prophet described.

1646
01:19:18.099 --> 01:19:19.701
A blinding white light.

1647
01:19:19.801 --> 01:19:23.338
clouds. but not Heaven.
a sense of wanting to return.

1648
01:19:23.438 --> 01:19:26.108
a feeling that my state
of reality wasn't real.

1649
01:19:28.109 --> 01:19:29.711
That wasn't a prophecy.

1650
01:19:30.579 --> 01:19:33.950
That was a near-death
experience.

1651
01:19:34.050 --> 01:19:35.350
When the oxygen
leaves your brain

1652
01:19:35.450 --> 01:19:38.020
or your heart stops pumping.
your mind

1653
01:19:38.119 --> 01:19:39.889
creates unbelievable things.

1654
01:19:39.989 --> 01:19:43.391
I think you've been
keeping this woman

1655
01:19:43.491 --> 01:19:45.527
on the edge of death
in order to ask her questions

1656
01:19:45.627 --> 01:19:48.030
about meaningless
hallucinations

1657
01:19:48.130 --> 01:19:50.365
so that you can substantiate
your idea

1658
01:19:50.465 --> 01:19:53.768
of what the one.
true religion really is.

1659
01:19:54.971 --> 01:19:56.805
MR. REED: Did you know...

1660
01:19:56.907 --> 01:19:57.873
that when you remember
something.

1661
01:19:57.974 --> 01:19:59.041
you're really only remembering

1662
01:19:59.140 --> 01:20:00.809
the last time you remembered
that experience?

1663
01:20:02.611 --> 01:20:03.913
You're not actually
recalling the event.

1664
01:20:04.014 --> 01:20:08.249
So your memory of dying
at Taco Bell... (CHUCKLING)

1665
01:20:08.350 --> 01:20:09.384
...isn't really of dying.

1666
01:20:09.484 --> 01:20:11.319
it's of the memory
of the memory

1667
01:20:11.419 --> 01:20:12.989
of the memory
of the memory of the memory...

1668
01:20:13.090 --> 01:20:16.324
stop me... (CHUCKLES)
...of that event.

1669
01:20:16.425 --> 01:20:18.426
So you're remembering
a false correlation

1670
01:20:18.526 --> 01:20:20.195
with the experience
you've just witnessed.

1671
01:20:20.295 --> 01:20:24.300
But this.
this is happening right now!

1672
01:20:24.399 --> 01:20:27.435
That's why I think.
Sister Barnes. Sister Paxton.

1673
01:20:27.535 --> 01:20:29.371
that you really need
to pay attention

1674
01:20:29.471 --> 01:20:31.007
because I promise you...
(CHUCKLING)

1675
01:20:31.108 --> 01:20:32.875
...we're not talking
about a magic trick.

1676
01:20:34.142 --> 01:20:36.177
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1677
01:20:39.180 --> 01:20:40.248
No.

1678
01:20:40.349 --> 01:20:42.918
we're talking
about magic underwear...

1679
01:20:43.019 --> 01:20:44.486
-(SLASHING)
-(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1680
01:20:50.158 --> 01:20:51.426
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1681
01:20:55.264 --> 01:20:57.432
(INAUDIBLE SCREAMING)

1682
01:21:05.273 --> 01:21:07.509
(IMPERCEPTIBLE)

1683
01:21:12.313 --> 01:21:14.550
(INAUDIBLE SCREAMING)

1684
01:21:28.030 --> 01:21:30.032
(SCREAMING) Help me! Help!

1685
01:21:30.132 --> 01:21:31.934
(WIND GUSTING)

1686
01:21:36.139 --> 01:21:38.373
(SOBS)

1687
01:21:39.808 --> 01:21:40.976
(INHALES SHARPLY)

1688
01:21:43.079 --> 01:21:44.380
(SIGHS)

1689
01:21:47.016 --> 01:21:48.184
(EXHALES SHAKILY)

1690
01:21:48.283 --> 01:21:49.784
MR. REED:
She'll come back to us!

1691
01:21:50.920 --> 01:21:52.220
I promise!

1692
01:21:54.556 --> 01:21:56.691
Sister Paxton.
do not be scared!

1693
01:21:56.791 --> 01:21:57.893
She will rise again.

1694
01:21:58.660 --> 01:21:59.895
Challenge him.

1695
01:21:59.995 --> 01:22:00.963
Debate.

1696
01:22:01.663 --> 01:22:02.731
Challenge him.

1697
01:22:03.866 --> 01:22:05.633
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1698
01:22:08.971 --> 01:22:10.605
(FOOTSTEPS)

1699
01:22:10.706 --> 01:22:12.842
MR. REED: Come on. now.
Sister B.

1700
01:22:14.242 --> 01:22:16.011
Wakey-wakey!

1701
01:22:16.112 --> 01:22:17.479
-(WATER DRIPPING)
-Whoa. whoa. whoa.

1702
01:22:17.579 --> 01:22:19.181
whoa. whoa. whoa!
No. that's not it.

1703
01:22:19.280 --> 01:22:21.984
That's not it.
That's a... a mucky pup.

1704
01:22:22.084 --> 01:22:23.251
Let's have that.
(CHUCKLES)

1705
01:22:26.521 --> 01:22:28.490
Moments. It'll be moments.

1706
01:22:28.590 --> 01:22:29.925
Let's have one
of your drum rolls. yeah?

1707
01:22:32.794 --> 01:22:33.762
Whoop!

1708
01:22:37.133 --> 01:22:39.267
Hey! (SNIFFLES)

1709
01:22:42.438 --> 01:22:43.939
I'm very sorry.

1710
01:22:44.039 --> 01:22:45.673
Something is wrong.

1711
01:22:46.142 --> 01:22:47.742
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1712
01:22:47.843 --> 01:22:48.944
I'm now worried...

1713
01:22:50.980 --> 01:22:52.081
that she's not...

1714
01:22:52.181 --> 01:22:53.182
(BOX CUTTER OPENS)

1715
01:22:53.282 --> 01:22:54.516
...coming back to us.

1716
01:22:57.253 --> 01:22:58.286
Yeah.

1717
01:22:58.386 --> 01:22:59.855
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

1718
01:22:59.956 --> 01:23:01.123
Oh. yeah.

1719
01:23:01.224 --> 01:23:03.358
-(SOBS)
-MR. REED: Oh. yeah.

1720
01:23:06.795 --> 01:23:07.762
Yep.

1721
01:23:08.663 --> 01:23:09.631
Yep.

1722
01:23:10.199 --> 01:23:11.332
Yeah.

1723
01:23:11.432 --> 01:23:12.935
There it is.

1724
01:23:13.035 --> 01:23:14.270
(GRUNTS)

1725
01:23:14.369 --> 01:23:15.436
No. it isn't.

1726
01:23:15.537 --> 01:23:17.106
That was a vein.

1727
01:23:17.206 --> 01:23:18.306
(MR. REED GRUNTS)

1728
01:23:18.407 --> 01:23:20.109
(SQUELCHING)

1729
01:23:20.209 --> 01:23:22.945
A-ha! (CHUCKLES) A-ha.

1730
01:23:23.045 --> 01:23:24.947
(TENSE MUSIC BUILDS)

1731
01:23:26.248 --> 01:23:27.183
The implant.

1732
01:23:27.283 --> 01:23:29.819
This is why she can't
come back to us.

1733
01:23:30.886 --> 01:23:31.887
Take a look!

1734
01:23:32.822 --> 01:23:34.123
I'm very sorry.

1735
01:23:34.756 --> 01:23:37.960
But Sister Barnes.
she's a program.

1736
01:23:40.563 --> 01:23:42.497
She's not real.

1737
01:23:42.597 --> 01:23:44.332
Do you know what gave it away?

1738
01:23:44.800 --> 01:23:45.667
The candles.

1739
01:23:45.767 --> 01:23:48.436
What are you saying?
I don't understand.

1740
01:23:48.536 --> 01:23:50.371
No. no. I know.
I know. I know.

1741
01:23:51.006 --> 01:23:51.974
How could you?

1742
01:23:54.210 --> 01:23:55.978
(SHUDDERS)

1743
01:23:57.313 --> 01:23:59.648
Can you explain it to me?

1744
01:24:02.450 --> 01:24:05.386
Are you. Sister Paxton.

1745
01:24:05.486 --> 01:24:08.389
familiar with
the Daoist concept

1746
01:24:08.489 --> 01:24:10.292
of "The Butterfly Dream"?

1747
01:24:10.391 --> 01:24:11.994
PAXTON: A butterfly...

1748
01:24:12.094 --> 01:24:15.396
A butterfly flaps its wings
and causes a typhoon?

1749
01:24:15.496 --> 01:24:16.764
That is
"The Butterfly Effect."

1750
01:24:16.866 --> 01:24:19.367
Common mistake. No.
"The Butterfly Dream"...

1751
01:24:19.467 --> 01:24:20.768
(CLATTERING)

1752
01:24:20.870 --> 01:24:22.804
...concerns an ancient
Chinese philosopher

1753
01:24:22.905 --> 01:24:24.505
who asked himself
the following question.

1754
01:24:24.606 --> 01:24:26.808
-(OBJECT CLATTERS)
-"Was I a man dreaming

1755
01:24:26.909 --> 01:24:28.643
"I'm a butterfly.
or am I now..."

1756
01:24:28.743 --> 01:24:29.510
(THUD)

1757
01:24:29.611 --> 01:24:32.815
"...a butterfly dreaming
that I am a man?"

1758
01:24:32.916 --> 01:24:34.183
Come and sit down.

1759
01:24:34.283 --> 01:24:35.851
Come on.
(CLICKS TONGUE) Here.

1760
01:24:35.951 --> 01:24:36.952
(SIGHS)

1761
01:24:39.554 --> 01:24:41.623
(SCRAPING ON TABLE)

1762
01:24:44.827 --> 01:24:45.828
This is us.

1763
01:24:46.494 --> 01:24:48.297
You and me alone together.

1764
01:24:48.396 --> 01:24:49.597
That was Barnes.

1765
01:24:50.199 --> 01:24:51.399
Bye-bye. Barnes.

1766
01:24:52.268 --> 01:24:55.470
I have come
to a dark realization

1767
01:24:55.570 --> 01:24:58.706
that we exist inside
a simulation so advanced

1768
01:24:58.806 --> 01:25:01.576
that we cannot tell the
difference between real life

1769
01:25:02.543 --> 01:25:03.778
and artificial dream.

1770
01:25:03.880 --> 01:25:08.716
You heard the Prophet.
She said. "It is not real."

1771
01:25:08.817 --> 01:25:11.653
You see. fire dynamics
are very difficult to render.

1772
01:25:11.753 --> 01:25:14.356
I've noticed this anomaly
in its behavior

1773
01:25:14.456 --> 01:25:16.557
when it interacts
with simulated NPCs.

1774
01:25:16.658 --> 01:25:19.661
like poor old Sister B.

1775
01:25:19.761 --> 01:25:23.399
She couldn't come back to us.
but when you die.

1776
01:25:23.498 --> 01:25:28.370
finger. please.
you will pass through death

1777
01:25:28.503 --> 01:25:30.572
-and wake up...
-(BOX CUTTER RATTLES)

1778
01:25:30.672 --> 01:25:32.074
...into the real world.

1779
01:25:32.474 --> 01:25:33.943
What do you think?

1780
01:25:34.043 --> 01:25:35.443
Yes. no. maybe?

1781
01:25:36.912 --> 01:25:37.980
Um...

1782
01:25:40.883 --> 01:25:42.450
That's a theory.

1783
01:25:43.919 --> 01:25:45.688
Well yeah.
you're very welcome to...

1784
01:25:46.788 --> 01:25:48.489
to challenge my premise.
I love that.

1785
01:25:50.525 --> 01:25:51.927
-(BOX CUTTER CLOSES)
-Go for it.

1786
01:25:52.027 --> 01:25:53.862
(SNIFFLING)

1787
01:25:56.698 --> 01:25:59.835
I don't think
this is a microchip.

1788
01:26:00.568 --> 01:26:01.536
MR. REED: Oh?

1789
01:26:01.636 --> 01:26:04.605
I think it's a contraceptive.

1790
01:26:06.507 --> 01:26:09.644
A... a birth control implant.

1791
01:26:11.180 --> 01:26:12.181
Huh.

1792
01:26:13.715 --> 01:26:15.985
Tell me. have you ever met

1793
01:26:16.085 --> 01:26:18.753
a Mormon missionary
who was on birth control?

1794
01:26:20.555 --> 01:26:25.526
Did "Sister Barnes" say
she was on birth control?

1795
01:26:25.626 --> 01:26:27.130
PAXTON: Our church
would've made her

1796
01:26:27.229 --> 01:26:28.831
feel ashamed about it.

1797
01:26:28.931 --> 01:26:30.666
and she would've been
too embarrassed.

1798
01:26:31.666 --> 01:26:33.469
-Simulation theory is...
-Ah!

1799
01:26:33.568 --> 01:26:36.271
"Hypothesis." please.
Sorry. it doesn't matter.

1800
01:26:37.239 --> 01:26:39.675
Simulation hypothesis

1801
01:26:39.774 --> 01:26:42.710
is not testable. is it?

1802
01:26:43.979 --> 01:26:47.349
No. it's a matter of belief.
like any religion.

1803
01:26:47.449 --> 01:26:49.717
You either believe it.
green door.

1804
01:26:49.818 --> 01:26:51.652
or you don't believe it.
purple door.

1805
01:26:52.688 --> 01:26:55.257
With all due respect.

1806
01:26:56.492 --> 01:26:57.658
I...

1807
01:26:58.260 --> 01:27:00.130
I don't believe it.

1808
01:27:00.896 --> 01:27:04.766
I'm not smart enough
to say why. I just don't.

1809
01:27:04.867 --> 01:27:07.169
Do you believe the miracle
that I showed you?

1810
01:27:07.970 --> 01:27:08.770
PAXTON: Yes.

1811
01:27:08.871 --> 01:27:10.639
-Yeah?
-PAXTON: At first.

1812
01:27:12.341 --> 01:27:13.641
But now?

1813
01:27:13.741 --> 01:27:16.211
I think something
happened tonight

1814
01:27:16.311 --> 01:27:18.347
that you didn't expect.

1815
01:27:18.447 --> 01:27:20.050
It feels like
you're improvising.

1816
01:27:20.149 --> 01:27:22.650
trying to convince me
of a simulation theory

1817
01:27:22.750 --> 01:27:24.887
that's not sticking.
Am I right?

1818
01:27:27.789 --> 01:27:31.060
Uh. (CHUCKLES) are you
asking me if you're right

1819
01:27:31.160 --> 01:27:32.127
that I am improvising

1820
01:27:32.227 --> 01:27:35.596
or you're right
that the simulation narrative

1821
01:27:35.697 --> 01:27:36.631
is not sticking?

1822
01:27:36.731 --> 01:27:39.168
-Yes.
-(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1823
01:27:41.970 --> 01:27:43.206
High-five.

1824
01:27:43.305 --> 01:27:45.307
(GRUNTS SOFTLY. CHUCKLES)

1825
01:27:46.542 --> 01:27:48.010
So. in fact.
you agree with your friend.

1826
01:27:48.110 --> 01:27:50.546
You think that the Prophet
was just hallucinating

1827
01:27:50.645 --> 01:27:52.780
a meaningless.
near-death experience.

1828
01:27:53.382 --> 01:27:54.516
No.

1829
01:27:55.150 --> 01:27:57.286
I think you switched
the bodies.

1830
01:27:57.386 --> 01:27:59.488
(MUSIC FADES OUT)

1831
01:27:59.587 --> 01:28:01.925
I just haven't
figured out how yet.

1832
01:28:03.724 --> 01:28:04.927
I switched...

1833
01:28:05.561 --> 01:28:06.829
the bodies?

1834
01:28:08.596 --> 01:28:09.832
(FIRE CRACKLING)

1835
01:28:12.201 --> 01:28:15.070
The doorbell rang
when the Elder got here.

1836
01:28:15.170 --> 01:28:18.108
-(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)
-(DOORBELL RINGING)

1837
01:28:18.207 --> 01:28:20.109
<i>Which drew our attention</i>
<i>to the stairs.</i>

1838
01:28:20.209 --> 01:28:22.810
<i>You would have been</i>
<i>prepared for that.</i>

1839
01:28:25.481 --> 01:28:26.782
When we came back downstairs.

1840
01:28:26.882 --> 01:28:30.519
I noticed the woman wasn't in
the same position as before.

1841
01:28:30.618 --> 01:28:32.387
It was similar...

1842
01:28:32.488 --> 01:28:33.422
PAXTON: <i>Her head is different.</i>

1843
01:28:33.523 --> 01:28:36.691
<i>But it was not the exact same.</i>

1844
01:28:36.791 --> 01:28:40.362
<i>I think another woman</i>
<i>who looked exactly like her</i>

1845
01:28:40.462 --> 01:28:41.630
<i>came into the basement</i>

1846
01:28:41.729 --> 01:28:43.932
<i>through a hidden door</i>
<i>or something.</i>

1847
01:28:44.032 --> 01:28:47.436
disposed of her body and then
took her place at the table.

1848
01:28:47.536 --> 01:28:48.570
I see.

1849
01:28:48.703 --> 01:28:51.573
And then.
once we got back downstairs.

1850
01:28:51.672 --> 01:28:55.844
<i>she read off</i>
<i>a scripted prophecy</i>

1851
01:28:55.944 --> 01:28:58.046
<i>that you prepared for her.</i>

1852
01:28:59.014 --> 01:29:02.783
<i>Except the last thing</i>
<i>she said was.</i>

1853
01:29:02.885 --> 01:29:04.186
<i>"It is not real."</i>

1854
01:29:04.286 --> 01:29:06.822
...not... real...

1855
01:29:06.922 --> 01:29:09.558
Maybe she was trying
to tell us

1856
01:29:09.657 --> 01:29:12.060
that the miracle wasn't real.

1857
01:29:13.929 --> 01:29:14.898
Ah.

1858
01:29:16.131 --> 01:29:17.765
You see what I mean when I say

1859
01:29:17.866 --> 01:29:20.202
something happened
that you didn't expect?

1860
01:29:20.302 --> 01:29:23.639
I think you gave her a script.
and she went off the book.

1861
01:29:23.738 --> 01:29:25.374
and now you're
trying to recover.

1862
01:29:27.543 --> 01:29:29.344
Well. if that's right.
then. uh.

1863
01:29:30.612 --> 01:29:33.215
there'd have to be another way
into this basement. yeah?

1864
01:29:34.316 --> 01:29:35.350
Shall we have a look?

1865
01:29:36.518 --> 01:29:38.686
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1866
01:29:42.791 --> 01:29:44.059
I don't think there is.

1867
01:29:44.660 --> 01:29:46.094
No.

1868
01:29:46.528 --> 01:29:48.331
I'm not doing very well.

1869
01:29:48.430 --> 01:29:49.865
Sister Paxton.

1870
01:29:50.300 --> 01:29:52.067
Unless...

1871
01:29:52.167 --> 01:29:53.202
(WATER DRIPPING)

1872
01:30:01.476 --> 01:30:03.478
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1873
01:30:11.119 --> 01:30:12.087
(RATTLING)

1874
01:30:21.331 --> 01:30:23.298
(WATER POURING)

1875
01:30:24.266 --> 01:30:26.235
(WATER DRAINING)

1876
01:30:38.648 --> 01:30:40.849
-(CLANKING)
-(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

1877
01:30:42.818 --> 01:30:44.987
(CREAKING)

1878
01:30:51.493 --> 01:30:53.028
Which means that...

1879
01:30:54.329 --> 01:30:55.796
there would have to be
a dead body down there

1880
01:30:55.898 --> 01:30:57.532
if you were right. huh?

1881
01:30:57.633 --> 01:30:59.001
PAXTON: Correct.

1882
01:30:59.701 --> 01:31:01.103
MR. REED: How will you
test your theory?

1883
01:31:01.737 --> 01:31:03.139
(SIGHS) I don't know.

1884
01:31:04.172 --> 01:31:06.708
MR. REED: But will you go
into that hole and

1885
01:31:06.807 --> 01:31:08.410
see if there's
somebody down there?

1886
01:31:08.510 --> 01:31:09.878
If I have to.

1887
01:31:10.712 --> 01:31:11.947
MR. REED: Why would you
do that?

1888
01:31:13.715 --> 01:31:16.652
Because I want
to know the truth.

1889
01:31:16.752 --> 01:31:19.021
and because the only way out
is through.

1890
01:31:20.255 --> 01:31:21.291
Robert Frost?

1891
01:31:21.923 --> 01:31:23.125
<i>Swamp Thing.</i>

1892
01:31:23.725 --> 01:31:25.127
(CHUCKLES)

1893
01:31:26.628 --> 01:31:28.063
Don't go into that cellar...

1894
01:31:29.898 --> 01:31:31.566
unless you are prepared

1895
01:31:31.667 --> 01:31:33.568
to discover the one.
true religion.

1896
01:31:33.669 --> 01:31:35.871
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1897
01:31:44.613 --> 01:31:46.814
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

1898
01:31:47.616 --> 01:31:48.984
(SNIFFLES)

1899
01:31:50.719 --> 01:31:52.854
(LADDER CREAKS)

1900
01:32:00.563 --> 01:32:02.532
(RISING SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC)

1901
01:32:06.935 --> 01:32:08.603
-(MUSIC STOPS)
-(SIGHS)

1902
01:32:08.704 --> 01:32:10.439
(FOOTSTEPS)

1903
01:32:17.913 --> 01:32:19.349
I knew it.

1904
01:32:19.448 --> 01:32:21.116
(DOOR CREAKS AND SLAMS)

1905
01:32:25.487 --> 01:32:27.689
(HEAVY BREATHING)

1906
01:32:27.789 --> 01:32:29.958
-(WATER SPLASHING)
-(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1907
01:32:37.599 --> 01:32:39.501
(LOCK CREAKS AND CLICKS)

1908
01:32:39.601 --> 01:32:41.436
(DOOR CREAKS)

1909
01:32:46.175 --> 01:32:48.343
(CONTINUES HEAVY BREATHING)

1910
01:32:53.115 --> 01:32:55.317
(UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1911
01:33:00.622 --> 01:33:02.358
(DOOR CREAKS)

1912
01:33:13.769 --> 01:33:15.337
(SHARP INHALE)

1913
01:33:16.905 --> 01:33:19.141
(DOOR CREAKING)

1914
01:33:24.514 --> 01:33:26.282
(WATER DRIPPING)

1915
01:33:28.750 --> 01:33:30.986
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1916
01:33:38.994 --> 01:33:41.197
(CONTINUES HEAVY BREATHING)

1917
01:33:46.134 --> 01:33:48.370
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1918
01:34:01.416 --> 01:34:02.684
(GASPS)

1919
01:34:02.784 --> 01:34:04.352
(HEAVY BREATHING)

1920
01:34:09.724 --> 01:34:11.326
(MUSIC FADES OUT)

1921
01:34:11.426 --> 01:34:13.361
(DOOR CREAKING)

1922
01:34:16.798 --> 01:34:17.733
(CLANK)

1923
01:34:17.834 --> 01:34:19.100
(DISTANT WEAK WHEEZING)

1924
01:34:19.201 --> 01:34:20.735
(SHUDDERING BREATH)

1925
01:34:20.837 --> 01:34:22.671
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

1926
01:34:32.380 --> 01:34:34.382
(COUGHING)

1927
01:34:34.917 --> 01:34:36.886
(FAINT GROANING)

1928
01:34:36.985 --> 01:34:39.354
(SHIVERING BREATH)

1929
01:34:44.392 --> 01:34:45.393
Hey.

1930
01:34:49.932 --> 01:34:51.233
(SNIFFLES)

1931
01:34:55.770 --> 01:34:56.738
(PAXTON SHIVERING)

1932
01:35:02.310 --> 01:35:04.212
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

1933
01:35:09.017 --> 01:35:10.752
Sorry about the cold.

1934
01:35:10.853 --> 01:35:12.053
(SNIFFLES)

1935
01:35:13.389 --> 01:35:14.689
Have you figured it out yet?

1936
01:35:14.789 --> 01:35:15.757
(PAXTON SNIFFLES)

1937
01:35:18.460 --> 01:35:19.661
I think so.

1938
01:35:21.663 --> 01:35:22.731
MR. REED: So what is it?

1939
01:35:23.933 --> 01:35:28.470
What is the one.
true religion. Sister P?

1940
01:35:28.570 --> 01:35:29.639
(PAXTON SHIVERING)

1941
01:35:29.738 --> 01:35:31.439
(SNIFFLING)

1942
01:35:31.541 --> 01:35:32.541
It's...

1943
01:35:35.978 --> 01:35:37.178
(INHALES)

1944
01:35:38.179 --> 01:35:39.681
(HEAVY BREATHING)

1945
01:35:39.782 --> 01:35:42.050
When we first arrived.

1946
01:35:42.150 --> 01:35:44.252
you left us alone
in your living room.

1947
01:35:44.352 --> 01:35:46.288
(DRAMATIC. SUSPENSEFUL
MUSIC PLAYING)

1948
01:35:46.389 --> 01:35:48.557
<i>We thought you were talking</i>
<i>to your wife.</i>

1949
01:35:48.657 --> 01:35:51.092
<i>but you were doing</i>
<i>something else.</i>

1950
01:35:51.894 --> 01:35:53.194
I was.

1951
01:35:53.295 --> 01:35:56.231
PAXTON: You took a key
from Sister Barnes' coat.

1952
01:35:56.331 --> 01:35:59.701
went outside to unlock
our bikes and hide them.

1953
01:36:04.206 --> 01:36:06.541
<i>I noticed your hair was wet</i>
<i>when you came back</i>

1954
01:36:06.641 --> 01:36:09.744
<i>with the drinks. like you were</i>
<i>out in the storm.</i>

1955
01:36:09.845 --> 01:36:11.646
You did this. I assume.
because you didn't want

1956
01:36:11.746 --> 01:36:12.514
the Elder to find our bikes

1957
01:36:12.614 --> 01:36:13.849
when he came back
looking for us.

1958
01:36:13.950 --> 01:36:15.083
(LATCH CLANKS)

1959
01:36:15.183 --> 01:36:16.785
But there was something else
on your mind.

1960
01:36:16.886 --> 01:36:17.887
(WATER POURING)

1961
01:36:17.987 --> 01:36:20.088
-There was.
-(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1962
01:36:21.590 --> 01:36:22.992
PAXTON: <i>You returned</i>
<i>the bike key</i>

1963
01:36:23.091 --> 01:36:25.327
<i>to the wrong coat pocket.</i>

1964
01:36:26.094 --> 01:36:28.030
<i>We thought this was a mistake</i>
<i>you made.</i>

1965
01:36:28.130 --> 01:36:29.297
(MOUTHING) Key.

1966
01:36:30.733 --> 01:36:32.667
PAXTON: (VOICE SHAKING)
But now I know it wasn't.

1967
01:36:32.767 --> 01:36:34.070
Why?

1968
01:36:34.169 --> 01:36:35.270
(INHALES)

1969
01:36:35.370 --> 01:36:38.608
You gave the bike lock
to one of your prophets.

1970
01:36:38.707 --> 01:36:42.177
instructed them to lock
the final cellar door with it.

1971
01:36:42.277 --> 01:36:45.347
But why. why. why?
Why did I do that?

1972
01:36:46.247 --> 01:36:48.183
Because you wanted me to know

1973
01:36:48.283 --> 01:36:51.152
the only reason
I'm standing here right now

1974
01:36:51.252 --> 01:36:52.989
is because it is exactly

1975
01:36:53.090 --> 01:36:55.256
where you want me
to be standing.

1976
01:36:56.157 --> 01:36:58.393
I'm not here
because I chose to be.

1977
01:36:58.493 --> 01:37:00.831
I'm here because you made me
choose to be.

1978
01:37:00.930 --> 01:37:02.264
Oh.

1979
01:37:02.364 --> 01:37:06.701
Because you want me to believe
the one. true religion is...

1980
01:37:06.801 --> 01:37:08.603
(SIGHS)

1981
01:37:08.703 --> 01:37:09.905
...control.

1982
01:37:13.976 --> 01:37:15.744
(CHUCKLES)

1983
01:37:15.845 --> 01:37:17.445
That is exactly right.

1984
01:37:19.715 --> 01:37:22.885
Religion is just
a system of control...

1985
01:37:23.585 --> 01:37:25.186
(WHEEZING)

1986
01:37:25.286 --> 01:37:27.023
(HEAVY BREATHING)
It's okay.

1987
01:37:27.123 --> 01:37:28.356
I'll help you.

1988
01:37:28.456 --> 01:37:29.691
MR. REED: No. you see.
that's what's so interesting.

1989
01:37:29.791 --> 01:37:31.593
They don't want your help.

1990
01:37:31.693 --> 01:37:33.695
They... (CHUCKLING)
they are exactly

1991
01:37:33.795 --> 01:37:34.864
where they chose to be.

1992
01:37:34.965 --> 01:37:36.331
But you killed that woman.

1993
01:37:36.431 --> 01:37:37.532
MR. REED: I disagree.

1994
01:37:37.632 --> 01:37:40.069
She... She chose to eat
a poisoned pie

1995
01:37:40.168 --> 01:37:42.104
because of her profound faith.

